//! Fixed-budget retypes of the slot dispatcher.
//!
//! The budget induction for `hnf3` can construct `slot_res` at its own budget
//! and below — never at *every* budget at once. But the dispatcher chain binds
//! `slot_res` with `forall (k1 : Nat)`, so the polymorphic premise is
//! **unsuppliable from inside the recursion**.
//!
//! The bodies need nothing: all eight `slot_res` applications in
//! `hnf3_app_residual_slot_dispatch` already receive its own `k0`. Only the
//! binder moves, so these proof terms are the originals verbatim.
//!
//! Added **alongside** the originals rather than replacing them. In-place edits
//! to proved declarations are the failure mode that broke `def_eq_fuel_of_struct`
//! earlier in this programme and had to be reverted.
//!
//! **The chain is complete.** `hnf3_app_residual_covered_slot_narrowed`
//! delegates to `hnf3_app_residual_covered` (`rigid_bridge.rs`), which takes a
//! budget-polymorphic residual of its own — so the retype ran one level further
//! up than first mapped. All four are here, and
//! `hnf3_app_residual_covered_slot_narrowed_at` is the entry point the budget
//! induction applies.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

use crate::spec::error::SpecError;
use crate::spec::Specification;

